// `sum`, `min`, `max` and `join` read the same three kinds as the rest of the
// family. Summing bytes is a checksum, and `min` uses the ordering `sort` uses, so
// `min("cba")` and `first(sort("cba"))` agree — they did not before, because
// `min` of a string was `none`.
^ ⟨
  sum_of_bytes: sum(bytes("ab")),
  min_of_a_string: min("cba"),
  max_of_a_string: max("cba"),
  min_agrees_with_sort: min("cba") = first(sort("cba")),
  join_characters: join("abc", "-"),
  empty_has_no_minimum: min([]) ?? "none"
⟩
